{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"StartFraction 1 Over 4 x y EndFraction plus x y z equals StartFraction 1 Over 3 y z EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given equation, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"z\"><mi>z</mi>\n</math> are positive numbers. Which expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>?</p>", "keys": ["9fffdaab-164a-4e6e-9e6a-426278a25eb2"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "0607f567-e47f-449d-a5a2-8c4251aa5d8e", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 4 x minus 3 z Over 12 x squared z squared EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"}, {"id": "9fffdaab-164a-4e6e-9e6a-426278a25eb2", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"StartRoot StartFraction 4 x minus 3 z Over 12 x squared z squared EndFraction EndRoot\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p>"}, {"id": "c56e4dd0-2ad8-4a0e-a5f2-2819f37625ba", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 1 Over 3 x z squared minus 4 x squared z EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"}, {"id": "17650a6b-3e2a-4654-b402-7f7826f347a2", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"StartRoot StartFraction 1 Over 3 x z squared minus 4 x squared z EndFraction EndRoot\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 1 Over 4 x y EndFraction plus x y z equals StartFraction 1 Over 3 y z EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"z\"><mi>z</mi></math> are positive numbers. Multiplying both sides of this equation by the least common denominator of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"12 x y z\"><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"12 x y z left parenthesis StartFraction 1 Over 4 x y EndFraction plus x y z right parenthesis equals 12 x y z left parenthesis StartFraction 1 Over 3 y z EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>, which gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 12 x y z Over 4 x y EndFraction plus 12 x squared y squared z squared equals StartFraction 12 x y z Over 3 y z EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 z plus 12 x squared y squared z squared equals 4 x\"><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 z\"><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"12 x squared y squared z squared equals 4 x minus 3 z\"><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"12 x squared z squared\"><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y squared equals StartFraction 4 x minus 3 z Over 12 x squared z squared EndFraction\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals plus or minus StartRoot StartFraction 4 x minus 3 z Over 12 x squared z squared EndFraction EndRoot\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>. Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> is a positive number, the expression <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartRoot StartFraction 4 x minus 3 z Over 12 x squared z squared EndFraction EndRoot\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math> is equivalent to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "78178dc9-f607-45b8-919f-337b38be824a", "correct_answer": ["B"]}